Discovery workflow (repeat per token)

Go to https://birdeye.so/solana/find-gems → "Trending" → sort by 24h %. Consider all trending tokens that at least doubled (>100%) in the last 24h. Start with the top ~10.
For each token's page, click the "Top Traders" tab, then apply the "Smart Money" filter. Optionally sort by Total PnL descending.
Read the table (use get_page_text and/or document.querySelectorAll('a[href*="/wallet-analyzer/"]') to pull FULL addresses — never use truncated addresses; they won't resolve).
For each worthwhile wallet, open https://birdeye.so/solana/wallet-analyzer/[FULL_ADDRESS] and read its LIFETIME Total PnL and age.

Qualification criteria (a wallet QUALIFIES if all are true)

Lifetime Total PnL (from the wallet-analyzer page, not the per-token table) is significantly positive.
Multiple multi-x wins (count of >100% and >500% trades). Several multi-x wins is more valuable than one big win.
Pattern of entering early and exiting with multi-x profits. Small caps / new mints are fine ($200 profit on $400 counts).
NOT brand new — exclude wallets only a few days old (roughly 1 week minimum; 1+ month preferred).
Classified as Smart Money by Birdeye.

Exclude / ignore

Exclude: brand-new wallets, pure market-maker/HFT bots, and wallets with negative lifetime PnL (you may log these in a separate EXCLUDED section for reference, but don't treat them as candidates).
Ignore win rate entirely (lots of small losses are fine).
Ignore SOL in PnL calculations.

Tags & clusters (important)

Log whether each wallet is Smart Money / Sniper / Builder (any that apply).
CLUSTERS ARE THE MOST VALUABLE SIGNAL. When several wallets co-buy a token within ~15 minutes, capture the FULL address of EVERY member of the cluster and give them a shared cluster tag (e.g., "TOKEN-cluster-A"). Do NOT collapse a cluster into one wallet — log every member as its own row. This is critical.
For cluster co-buyers where you only captured per-token PnL (not lifetime), mark the PnL with an asterisk and note "*per-token PnL; lifetime TBV" so I know it still needs lifetime verification.

De-duplication (ONE ROW PER WALLET, append-only)

Before adding a wallet, read SOL_early_token_traders.txt and collect every FULL address already present. Only append wallets whose address is NOT already in the file. Do NOT add "UPDATED" rows, and do NOT edit or re-add existing wallets — if a wallet is already listed, skip it entirely. One row per wallet, forever.
Why: an automated ingestion script reads this file into the bot's wallet pool and de-dupes by address, so duplicate or "UPDATED" rows are ignored anyway. And lifetime-PnL changes on an already-listed wallet don't matter — once ingested, the bot scores each wallet by its LIVE cluster behavior (does it co-buy winning tokens with other tracked wallets?), not by the curated PnL number. So PnL is only a coarse entry filter here, not the thing that earns a wallet its place. Keep the bar where the prompt already sets it; don't tighten it into a high PnL floor (big-PnL wallets are often funds/treasuries that don't generate usable signals).

